# ===== A+ Studio backend — environment =====
# Copy to `backend/.env` (gitignored) or set these in Render's dashboard / env group.
# Real environment variables always win over this file.
#
# One-time setup in Google Cloud Console (console.cloud.google.com):
#  1. Create a project (or pick one). This project is INTERNAL to the curefit.com Workspace,
#     which is why the restricted drive.readonly scope needs no Google app verification.
#  2. APIs & Services -> Enable APIs: "Google Sheets API" and "Google Drive API".
#  3. OAuth consent screen -> User type "Internal".
#  4. Credentials -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application.
#     Authorised redirect URIs:  http://localhost:8787/auth/callback
#                                https://<your-service>.onrender.com/auth/callback
#  5. Copy the Client ID and Client secret below.

# ---- required: Google sign-in --------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional — defaults to http://localhost:<PORT>/auth/callback. On Render this MUST be the
# full https URL and MUST exactly match one of the Authorised redirect URIs above.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8787/auth/callback

# ---- required in production: session sealing -------------------------------------------------
# The Google refresh token is sealed with AES-256-GCM under this key and handed to the plugin as
# its opaque session string, so sign-ins survive a Render redeploy (Render's disk is ephemeral).
#   generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# If unset, a random key is made at boot and EVERY SIGN-IN DIES ON RESTART (the server warns).
# Rotating this value signs everyone out — that is the only revocation lever, so treat it like a
# database password: secret env var only, never committed, never logged.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ---- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=8787

# Belt-and-braces disk mirror of in-flight sessions. Leave UNSET on Render: sealed tokens are the
# real persistence and a persistent disk pins the service to one instance. Set it only if you have
# actually mounted a writable disk, e.g. SESSION_DIR=/var/data
# SESSION_DIR=

# ffmpeg, for POST /api/compose. The Docker image installs it at /usr/bin/ffmpeg and these can
# stay unset. Set them if you run `node server.js` directly with ffmpeg somewhere unusual.
# FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg
# FFPROBE_PATH=ffprobe
# APLUS_TMP_DIR=/tmp/aplus
# COMPOSE_TIMEOUT_MS=300000          # hard kill for a single ffmpeg pass (ms)
# COMPOSE_MAX_INPUT_BYTES=67108864   # 64 MB per decoded input (the PNG, the GIF)
# COMPOSE_MAX_PIXELS=40000000        # refuse an output canvas bigger than this (width x height)
# MAX_BODY_BYTES=100663296           # 96 MB request body cap (base64 inflates by ~33%)
# MAX_DRIVE_DOWNLOAD_BYTES=67108864  # 64 MB cap on a Drive file download

# AI-assisted template labelling (docs/add-to-template-plan.md). NOT IMPLEMENTED YET — this is
# env plumbing only, so the key has somewhere to live when it is.
# !! NEVER put this key in plugin/ or plugin-src/. Plugin code ships as a readable file; anything
# !! in it is public. The plugin calls this backend, and only this backend calls Anthropic.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
